<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Embark on a 15-day odyssey following the footsteps of ancient Silk Road traders from Kashgar in China's far west to Tashkent, the heart of Central Asia. This perfectly paced journey combines the rugged beauty of Xinjiang with the architectural splendor of Uzbekistan's legendary cities. From the Sunday Market in Kashgar to the turquoise domes of Samarkand and the ancient streets of Bukhara, every day reveals a new chapter in the Silk Road story.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Experience Kashgar's legendary Sunday Market</li><li>Explore the Kizil Thousand Buddha Caves near Kuqa</li><li>Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins in Turpan</li><li>Marvel at Registan Square in Samarkand</li><li>Wander through Bukhara's UNESCO Old City</li><li>See the world's oldest Quran in Tashkent</li><li>Ride high-speed trains through Central Asia</li><li>Discover the Karez irrigation system</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Kashgar</h4><p>Your guide meets you at Kashgar Airport. Transfer to hotel. Evening walk through the Old City.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market &amp; Old City</h4><p>Explore the legendary Sunday Market. Visit Id Kah Mosque and the maze-like alleys of the Old City. Afternoon at Abakh Khoja Tomb.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar → Kuqa (Train)</h4><p>Train journey to the ancient oasis city of Kuqa. Visit the Kizil Thousand Buddha Caves, one of the earliest Buddhist cave complexes in China.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kuqa 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kuqa — Tianshan Grand Canyon</h4><p>Explore the dramatic Tianshan Grand Canyon with its towering red rock formations. Afternoon visit to the Kuqa Grand Mosque and old town.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kuqa 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kuqa → Turpan (Train)</h4><p>Train to Turpan, the second-lowest depression on Earth. Afternoon visit to the ancient Jiaohe Ruins, a spectacular city carved from raw earth.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan — Flaming Mountains &amp; Grape Valley</h4><p>Visit the Flaming Mountains, Karez underground irrigation system, and lush Grape Valley. Enjoy a traditional Uyghur lunch with local families.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan → Urumqi</h4><p>Drive to Urumqi. Visit the Xinjiang Regional Museum. Afternoon at Hongshan Park for panoramic city views and the Grand Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi ✈ Tashkent</h4><p>Morning flight to Tashkent. Upon arrival, explore Amir Timur Square and enjoy a welcome dinner at a traditional Uzbek restaurant.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent City Tour</h4><p>Visit the Khast Imam Complex, home of the world's oldest Quran. Explore Chorsu Bazaar and admire the ornate Soviet-era metro stations.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent → Samarkand (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Take the Afrosiyob train to Samarkand. Visit the magnificent Registan Square, Gur-e-Amir Mausoleum, and Bibi-Khanym Mosque.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Samarkand 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand — Shah-i-Zinda &amp; Silk Road Heritage</h4><p>Explore the necropolis of Shah-i-Zinda, Ulugh Beg Observatory, and a traditional silk paper workshop. Free time at Siab Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Samarkand 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand → Bukhara (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Train to Bukhara. Explore the Old City: Lyab-i Hauz plaza, the Ark Citadel, and the towering Kalon Minaret.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bukhara 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara — Full Day Exploration</h4><p>Full day discovering Bukhara: Samanid Mausoleum, Chor Minor, Bolo Hauz Mosque, and the old trading domes. Evening folk performance with dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Bukhara 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara → Tashkent (High-Speed Train)</h4><p>Return to Tashkent by high-speed train. Afternoon free for last-minute exploration or shopping. Farewell dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Tashkent 4★</span><span>🍽 B/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Tashkent</h4><p>Transfer to Tashkent International Airport. Your Great Silk Road journey concludes. Safe travels!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

